╭─ ☤ Hermes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
- NemoClaw is an open-source reference stack for running qualified AI agents (OpenClaw, Hermes, LangChain Deep Agents Code) more safely inside NVIDIA OpenShell sandboxes, providing guided onboarding, managed inference, network policy, and lifecycle operations
- It installs and configures OpenShell (part of NVIDIA Agent Toolkit) with credential custody for managed inference and applies the selected agent integration layer and versioned blueprint, keeping qualification-only candidates separate from supported runtimes
- NemoClaw supports multiple inference providers (local vLLM/Ollama, NVIDIA Endpoints, OpenRouter, OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, Model Router) and includes platform-specific quickstarts for DGX Spark, DGX Station, and Windows WSL, with a single-command installer (curl -fsSL https://www.nvidia.com/nemoclaw.sh | bash)
